      ⍝ Regression. M. Hall Jan. 27. 2025
      ⍝
      )ERASE FOO

      ⊣⎕FX 'FOO' '10' '20'
      ∇FOO[1]123∇
      FOO
123
20

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(c)): a bad local variable in a ∇ header
      ⍝ (not a name) used to unconditionally leak an internal debug
      ⍝ trace (the raw offending Token) to the session; only the
      ⍝ returned message string is supposed to be reported.
      ⍝
      ∇Z←F B;1
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇Z←F B;1
             ^

      )MORE
Bad function header: Bad local variable (not a name)

      ⍝ regression (Bugs28 #100(y)): ∇FOO[∆3]∇ (delete line 3 on the
      ⍝ opening ∇ line itself) was a DEFN ERROR because is_axis()
      ⍝ (Nabla.cc) accepted [∆3] as a bracket-axis purely on its shape
      ⍝ (∆ is a legal identifier-start character and a digit-only
      ⍝ suffix is a legal continuation, so "∆3" parses as one ordinary
      ⍝ name) -- pre-empting parse_oper(), which already handles [∆N]
      ⍝ correctly once inside an open editing session. A bracket-axis
      ⍝ is only ever valid on a header that also has a right argument B
      ⍝ (UserFunction_header.cc's init_signature() only recognises [X]
      ⍝ after first stripping a trailing B), so is_axis() now also
      ⍝ requires something to follow ']' before accepting it as an
      ⍝ axis, deferring to parse_oper() otherwise.
      ⍝
      )ERASE ZZ100Y
      ∇ZZ100Y
line1
line2
line3
      ∇

      ∇ZZ100Y[⎕]∇
    ∇
[0]   ZZ100Y
[1]   line1
[2]   line2
[3]   line3
    ∇  ³

      ∇ZZ100Y[∆3]∇

      ∇ZZ100Y[⎕]∇
    ∇
[0]   ZZ100Y
[1]   line1
[2]   line2
    ∇  ³

      ⍝ control: an out-of-range delete target is still correctly
      ⍝ rejected (as DEFN ERROR, via the same unified ∇-open error
      ⍝ path), leaving the function untouched
      ⍝
      ∇ZZ100Y[∆99]∇
DEFN ERROR+
      ∇ZZ100Y[∆99]∇
                  ^

      ∇ZZ100Y[⎕]∇
    ∇
[0]   ZZ100Y
[1]   line1
[2]   line2
    ∇  ³

      ⍝ control: the pre-existing working forms (multi-line-number and
      ⍝ dash-range deletes) are unaffected
      ⍝
      ∇ZZ100Y[1∆2]∇

      ∇ZZ100Y[⎕]∇
    ∇
[0]   ZZ100Y
    ∇  ³

      )ERASE ZZ100Y

      ⍝ control: a genuine axis header (with a real B) is unaffected
      ⍝
      )ERASE ZZ100G
      ∇Z←ZZ100G[X]B
Z←X+B
      ∇

      ZZ100G[2] 3
5

